    "state": "APPROVED",
    "body": "Reviewed and verified locally (fork PRs don't get a CI run here): `tsc --noEmit` clean, `eslint src` clean, full suite green (631 tests), merges onto `main` alongside #356/#359 with no conflicts.\n\nPicking this over my own #360, and the deciding factor is the legacy recovery — parsing `const PORT = N;` out of the old `compass-server.js` and migrating it into the port file means anyone with a visualizer already running when they upgrade gets a real answer instead of being told to restart. Mine just gave up in that case. `removeCompassState()` and the `pid <= 0` hardening in `readAlivePid` are both improvements on what was there.\n\nThe tests are the other reason: driving the real command against a temp `IX_HOME` with `spawn`/`net` mocked, asserting output *and* file state, catches wiring mistakes that my pure-function tests would have sailed straight past.\n\nTwo small things from #360 I will port as a follow-up rather than block on:\n\n1. When `-p` does not match the running port, say so. Right now the correct URL prints but the user never learns their `-p` was ignored — worth using `getOptionValueSource(\"port\")` so an explicit `-p 8080` warns and a bare `ix view` stays quiet.\n2. `ix view status` could print the URL now that the port is recorded.",
